No. Multiplication of two monetary values is generally not meaningful for a billing counter.

For example:

Addition is useful for calculating total bills.
Subtraction is useful for calculating balances.
Comparison is useful for checking amounts.
Multiplication by a quantity or tax rate can be useful, but multiplying one Money object by another Money object is not appropriate.
Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis Instead of member functions, operators can be implemented as non-member friend functions.
Example: friend Money operator+(const Money& a, const Money& b) { Money result; result.paise = a.paise + b.paise; return result; }

Named functions can also be used: Money add(Money a, Money b) { return Money(0, 0); // Illustrative only }

